# Code owners for PulseStream.
#
# Every path here gets an automatic review request, and - once branch protection
# requires review from code owners - cannot be merged without one. The point is
# not ceremony: these are the paths where a wrong change is either invisible in
# review or expensive to undo. A workflow edit can exfiltrate a token, a
# manifest edit can take the platform down, and a change to this file can remove
# every other rule in it.
#
# Later rules win over earlier ones, so the catch-all comes first and the
# narrowest, most sensitive paths come last.
#
# Ownership currently sits with a single maintainer. When that changes, split
# these lines by area rather than adding everyone to every line - a review
# request that always goes to everybody is a review request nobody answers.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                                       @ME-Massine

# Services: the application code and its dependency manifests.
/services/                              @ME-Massine

# Build and release automation. These workflows hold GITHUB_TOKEN permissions,
# publish images, and sign them; a change here changes what the project ships
# and what credentials that process can reach.
/.github/workflows/                     @ME-Massine

# Repository automation and policy: Dependabot coverage, code ownership itself,
# templates.
/.github/                               @ME-Massine

# Deployment topology: Kubernetes manifests, NetworkPolicies, Kafka, and the
# local Docker Compose stack.
/infrastructure/                        @ME-Massine

# Validation scripts. CI runs these, so a change here changes what CI is
# actually proving.
/scripts/                               @ME-Massine

# Architecture decision records are the project's memory. Amending one silently
# rewrites the reasoning behind a decision that is already in effect.
/docs/decisions/                        @ME-Massine

# Supply-chain surface. Each of these decides what the release pipeline trusts:
# the accepted-vulnerability list, the reporting policy, and the Maven
# distribution checksum every build verifies before executing Maven.
/.trivyignore.yaml                      @ME-Massine
/SECURITY.md                            @ME-Massine
/services/*/.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties  @ME-Massine
